  <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100"><div class="row gy-4 align-items-center"><div class="col-lg-6"><img src="/assets/img/Smoky Mountain Acres/Khatadin.webp" class="img-fluid" alt="Katahdin sheep at Smoky Mountain Acres"></div><div class="col-lg-6 content"><h2>Katahdin Sheep</h2><p>Our Katahdin sheep bring a hardy, traditional presence to the farm. They are grazing animals, so pasture is not just enrichment for them; it is central to how they are designed to eat.</p><p>They are handled and observed as part of daily farm care. As the flock grows, we will share more about individual animals, lambs, breeding plans, and future availability.</p><a href="/Our-Animals/" class="offer-link">BACK TO OUR ANIMALS</a></div></div></div>
