<section id="sheep-grazing" class="services section">
  <div class="container section-title" data-aos="fade-up"><div class="section-title-row"><img class="text-decoration-left" src="/assets/img/Smoky Mountain Acres/text-decoration-half-leaf.webp" alt=""><h2>GRAZING AND SEASONAL CARE</h2><img class="text-decoration-right" src="/assets/img/Smoky Mountain Acres/text-decoration-half-leaf.webp" alt=""></div><p>Sheep help us pay close attention to forage, weather, and the condition of the land.</p></div>
  <div class="container"><div class="row gy-4 justify-content-center"><div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6"><div class="offer-item text-center"><i class="bi bi-flower1 offer-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i><h3>Forage First</h3><p>Sheep graze grasses, clover, broadleaf plants, and other suitable forage as they move through pasture.</p></div></div><div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6"><div class="offer-item text-center"><i class="bi bi-cloud-sun offer-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i><h3>Seasonal Adjustments</h3><p>Pasture changes with weather and growth. Hay, minerals, or supplemental feed may be needed when conditions or animal needs require it.</p></div></div><div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6"><div class="offer-item text-center"><i class="bi bi-arrow-repeat offer-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i><h3>Pasture Management</h3><p>Moving animals and resting ground helps protect forage and spread the impact of grazing across the farm.</p></div></div></div></div>
</section>

<section id="sheep-availability" class="about section paper-texture"><div class="container" data-aos="fade-up"><div class="row gy-4 align-items-center"><div class="col-lg-5 order-lg-2"><img src="/assets/img/Smoky Mountain Acres/SMAView3.webp" class="img-fluid" alt="Pasture landscape near Smoky Mountain Acres"></div><div class="col-lg-7 order-lg-1 content"><h2>Future Lamb and Sheep Availability</h2><p>We are not currently listing sheep for sale. As the flock develops, future offerings may include lambs, breeding stock, or meat animals depending on our plans and the animals ready to leave the farm.</p><p>We will share clear information about availability, purpose, age, and care rather than treating every animal as an interchangeable product.</p><a href="/livestock/" class="cta-btn">View Livestock Updates</a></div></div></div></section>

